  <prompt>Implement the I5 concurrency guard per spec.md FR-23 + §4D. When a new provisioning run starts (POST /api/runs), the L2 control plane MUST attempt an optimistic upsert of `sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_currentrunid` from `null → newRunId` for the target customer's registry row. On conflict (row already has a non-null currentRunId belonging to a different run), the endpoint returns 409 Conflict to the caller with the winning run ID in the response body. On run completion / cancellation / failure, sprk_currentrunid MUST be cleared back to null. Cross-customer runs are unaffected — I5 is intentionally per-customer serialization only.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse alternate-key upserts, optimistic concurrency using Dataverse ETag semantics (If-Match / row-version), IDataverseService contract, and the L2 REST endpoint layer. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>File src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Concurrency/CustomerRunGuard.cs exists as ICustomerRunGuard with an implementation that: (a) TryAcquireAsync(customerId, runId) → returns success on null → newRunId, returns Conflict(winningRunId) on any existing non-null value; (b) ReleaseAsync(customerId, runId) → clears the column back to null iff the current value matches runId (no-op otherwise). POST /api/runs invokes TryAcquireAsync before enqueueing H0; on Conflict, returns 409 to caller with winningRunId in response body. Terminal-state handlers (H13 success, cancel, failure) invoke ReleaseAsync. Integration tests cover concurrent-acquire-conflict + terminal-state-release.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Per spec.md FR-23 + §4D I5 + design.md §4.2: the platform serializes runs per customer to prevent partial-state corruption when two concurrent provisions target the same environment. Cross-customer runs run in parallel — I5 does NOT globally serialize. sprk_currentrunid on the registry table is the single source of truth; task 023 defines the column; this task wires the guard around it.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Concurrency/CustomerRunGuard.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Concurrency/ICustomerRunGuard.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Concurrency/CustomerRunGuard.Tests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Api/RunsEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="023" status="pending">sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_currentrunid column exists (Wave C1)</dependency>
      <dependency task="058" status="pending">State-reconciler + Cosmos state store are in place</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-23">SCOPE: Same-customer runs are serialized via sprk_currentrunid optimistic upsert (null → newRunId); conflict = 409 with winning run ID; cross-customer runs are parallel.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec.md §4D I5">SCOPE: This guard implements one of the 5 binding tenant-isolation invariants — verified by the ArchTest suite (task 064).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">SCOPE: sprk_currentrunid GUID values follow the Dataverse GUID canonicalization contract (lowercase, no braces).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: Do NOT use a Redis lock or an in-memory lock as the primary guard — the guard MUST be durable across L2 instance restarts. The single source of truth is Dataverse sprk_currentrunid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: TryAcquireAsync is idempotent for the same (customerId, runId) tuple — a re-call with the same runId returns success without error, not conflict.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: ReleaseAsync clears the column ONLY IF the current value matches the caller's runId — protects against a stale caller clearing a different run's grab.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE: If the guard needs to consume IDataverseService, do NOT downcast (per r3 task 028) — use the UnwrapServiceClient extension.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Same-customer serialization via Dataverse optimistic concurrency on sprk_currentrunid</topic>
    <files>
