      <pattern name="Dataverse ETag / optimistic upsert" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs">Existing shape for If-Match / row-version-guarded Dataverse writes; copy for sprk_currentrunid guard.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Load spec.md FR-23 + §4D I5 + this project's CLAUDE.md.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Inventory">Read task 023 registry column definition. Grep RunsEndpoints.cs (task 057) for the enqueue path where TryAcquire must fire.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Interface">Author ICustomerRunGuard with TryAcquireAsync + ReleaseAsync signatures.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Implementation">Author CustomerRunGuard.cs — inject IDataverseService; TryAcquireAsync uses ETag-guarded update from null → newRunId; ReleaseAsync uses ETag-guarded update from newRunId → null with match check.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Endpoint wire">Modify RunsEndpoints.cs POST /api/runs to invoke TryAcquireAsync before enqueue; on Conflict, return 409 with winningRunId in response body.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Release path">Wire ReleaseAsync into terminal-state transitions: H13 success path, cancel-run path, failure/quarantine path (integrate with reconciler task 058 state transitions).</step>
    <step order="6" name="Tests">Author CustomerRunGuard.Tests.cs: (a) happy acquire; (b) concurrent-acquire returns Conflict with winning runId; (c) re-acquire with same runId is idempotent success; (d) release-match clears column; (e) release-mismatch is no-op.</step>
    <step order="7" name="ArchTest hook">Verify task 064 I5 ArchTest is aware of this guard as the sanctioned pattern.</step>
    <step order="8" name="Verify">dotnet build + dotnet test = green; dotnet format; zero analyzer warnings.</step>
    <step order="9" name="Index update">Update TASK-INDEX.md: task 059 → ✅.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Deviations">Document any deviation in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

