  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_currentrunid is null for customer C, when TryAcquireAsync(C, runA) is invoked, then result = Success and the column value = runA.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_currentrunid = runA for customer C, when TryAcquireAsync(C, runB) is invoked concurrently, then result = Conflict with winningRunId = runA; the column value remains runA.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_currentrunid = runA for customer C, when TryAcquireAsync(C, runA) is re-invoked (idempotent), then result = Success without conflict.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_currentrunid = runA, when ReleaseAsync(C, runA) is invoked, then the column is cleared to null.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given sprk_currentrunid = runA, when ReleaseAsync(C, runB) is invoked with mismatched runId, then the column remains runA (no-op).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cross-customer: TryAcquireAsync(C1, runX) + TryAcquireAsync(C2, runY) BOTH succeed (I5 is per-customer only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: POST /api/runs with a customerId that already has an in-flight run returns HTTP 409 Conflict with the winning runId in the JSON response body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0; zero analyzer warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Reference: spec.md FR-23 + §4D I5 + design.md §4.2. Consumed by task 060 (I6 crash recovery — released runs should be re-acquirable by the crash-recovery scan).</notes>

